Spec: DXF Import/Export

Purpose:
  Support DXF file format for interoperability with CAD software
  and laser control programs that prefer DXF over SVG.

Owns:
  ./dxf-import.ts
  ./dxf-export.ts
  ./dxf-import.test.ts
  ./dxf-export.test.ts

Must:
  Import DXF R12/R14 format (most compatible with laser software).
  Support LINE, ARC, CIRCLE, LWPOLYLINE, POLYLINE, SPLINE entities.
  Convert DXF entities to PathShape instances.
  Respect DXF units (assume mm unless INSUNITS header says otherwise).
  Export all shapes as DXF polylines with mm coordinates.
  Preserve layer assignment as DXF layers.

Must not:
  Support 3D DXF entities (only 2D).
  Support DXF blocks/inserts in initial implementation.
  Import hatches or dimensions.
  Depend on a heavy DXF parsing library (keep bundle small).

Depends on:
  @PathShape
  @IShape
  @useStore

Accepts:
  DXF file content (string)

Returns:
  IShape[] (imported shapes)
  string (exported DXF content)

Scenario: import simple DXF with polylines
  Given a DXF file containing 2 closed LWPOLYLINE entities
  When the user imports the file
  Then 2 closed PathShape instances appear on canvas
  And their coordinates match the DXF values in mm

Scenario: export shapes to DXF
  Given the canvas has 3 shapes (rect, circle, polygon)
  When the user exports as DXF
  Then a valid DXF R12 file is produced
  And it contains 3 entities with correct mm coordinates

Tasks:
  [ ] Research lightweight DXF parsing approach (custom parser vs dxf-parser lib).
  [ ] Implement DXF import for LINE entities.
  [ ] Implement DXF import for CIRCLE and ARC entities.
  [ ] Implement DXF import for LWPOLYLINE entities.
  [ ] Implement DXF export (shapes → LWPOLYLINE entities).
  [ ] Add DXF to the import file picker filter.
  [ ] Add "Export DXF" option in header.
  [ ] Add unit tests for import.
  [ ] Add unit tests for export round-trip.

Done when:
  DXF files from common laser software import correctly.
  Exported DXF opens in LightBurn/AutoCAD without errors.
  Round-trip preserves geometry within 0.01mm.
